  "representation": {
    "authority": "Resource scopes use the existing FinallyContext and Handler return target/slot. One context constructor captures lexical control and iterator boundaries; explicit and implicit finalizers share abrupt-exit path emission.",
    "transitions": "Store the return value, dispose the resource scope, then resume the enclosing return/finalizer. Break/continue select only enclosing scopes they actually leave; nested finalizers propagate the original destination. Generator return uses the existing handler metadata.",
    "invariants": "LIFO disposal; preserve returns and error identity/suppression; resource disposal precedes closing enclosing iterators; internal loop control does not leave outer resource scopes; uninitialized cleanup stacks cause neither disposal nor Await.",
    "scope": "Function/arrow bodies, nested blocks and classic for resource initializers. No new runtime-side map, serializer layout, representation ABI, guest shim, fixture branch or duplicated semantic unit test."
  },
  "contract": "https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/abstract-operations.html#sec-disposeresources",
